-5b2d-ee30-0eb8-906d092ff897","a813853d-bc69-9855-a0a0-d03ec0b8d3a4"],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"reset":false,"shade":true,"mirror_uv":false,"autouv":0,"isOpen":false,"primary_selected":false}],"textures":[{"name":"main_base_citadel.png","path":"","folder":"","namespace":"","id":"0","group":"","scope":0,"width":1024,"height":1024,"uv_width":1024,"uv_height":1024,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","file_format":"png","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","wrap_mode":"limited","pbr_channel":"color","fps":7,"frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"a551c42e-1d59-5cc4-bf9c-10d30efc2362","source":"data:image/png;base64,","relative_path":""}],"description":"# main_base_citadel\n\nMain base tier 4, the Citadel, with its engine platform (Patch 5; a variant of main_base_l10). The white-and-grey fortress of main_base_l10 with its pointed flag tower removed: the upper keep is widened into a massive square tower with corner buttresses and lit windows, and its top is a broad, flat, crenellated stone platform carried on three stepped courses of corbels. A fixed siege engine and its crew stand on the platform, or up to 4 units when it has no engine. The cannon muzzles in the bastion gun ports are gone (the ports remain as loopholes).\n\n- Footprint: 14 x 14 columns (224 x 224 units, 6.30 x 6.30 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -118..118, y 0..383 (platform deck 339, merlons 352, pennant 383), z -118..118 units.\n- Texture: 1024 x 1024, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering, flat pixel-art tones per material. 871 faces buried inside other cubes or on the ground carry no texture.\n- Cubes: finished 569, construction_0 44, construction_33 234, construction_66 371, ruined 210 (the state sets are cut from the finished cubes and map into the texture regions of the faces they were cut from).\n- Glowing parts: the keep's and upper keep's lit windows `glow_window_*` (main bases are always lit at night).\n- Team colour (52, 96, 178): the banners on the keep and gate, the platform banner and the corner pennant.\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and footing with materials waiting, then walls rising inside scaffold).\n- `ruined`: broken walls at uneven heights, rubble and fallen beams.\n- `main_base_citadel_damaged.png`: damaged texture (cracks, scorch) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- keep: 108 x 253 x 108 centred at x 0, z 12, with the upper keep 88 x 86 x 88 above it and the platform 104 x 13 x 104 on top (y 339 to 352)\n- curtain wall: 224 x 120 x 224 ring\n- bastions: 48 x 143 x 48 at the corners\n\n## Attachment points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_engine` at (0, 339, 12): the fixed siege engine, facing -Z, on the iron track hub.\n- `slot_crew_1` at (-20, 339, 40), `slot_crew_2` at (20, 339, 40): its artillery crewmen.\n- `slot_platform_1` to `slot_platform_4` at (-36, 339, -24), (36, 339, -24), (-36, 339, 48), (36, 339, 48): units on an empty platform.\n- `slot_parapet_1` to `slot_parapet_8` on the keep walk at y 253, unchanged from main_base_l10.\n- `slot_tower_1` to `slot_tower_4` at (±92, 135, ±92), `slot_gate` at (0, 0, -122), `slot_door` at (0, 0, -49), unchanged."}